{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"87c10415-c3ac-4cc7-b659-56d319aac03a","step_index":121,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"ntinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_tools.py#L90-L108).\n\n### Verification\n\nRun the test suite:\n```bash\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\nOutput:\n```\nRan 49 tests in 0.002s\n\nOK\n```\n","duration_seconds":10.445557,"usage":{"input_tokens":5136,"output_tokens":2457,"thinking_tokens":64,"cache_read_tokens":130410,"total_tokens":7593}}}
{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"87c10415-c3ac-4cc7-b659-56d319aac03a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Tests have been added to catch bugs encountered by real MCP clients, and the issues found in the server and tool implementations have been fixed.\n\n### Issues Identified \u0026 Fixed\n\n1. **Production `DynamoDB` / [`DynamoStore`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/db.py#L42-L55) Decimal Serialization Failure**:\n   - `DynamoStore` converts all numeric fields to `decimal.Decimal` at any depth. [`tools._coerce()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tools.py#L5-L26) previously only converted `word_count`, leaving `stats.views`, `stats.rating`, and `stats.revisions` as `Decimal` instances.\n   - When real clients requested [`get_note`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tools.py#L29-L33) in production (`PRODUCTION_DB=1`), standard `json.dumps()` crashed with `TypeError: Object of type Decimal is not JSON serializable`, causing every `get_note` call to fail with `isError: True`.\n   - **Fix**: Updated [`tools._coerce()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tools.py#L5-L26) to recursively coerce all Decimals into native JSON-compatible types (`int` for whole numbers and list items, `float` for ratings/fractional numbers).\n\n2. **Lifecycle Notification Handling (`notifications/initialized`)**:\n   - Standard MCP clients send a `notifications/initialized` notification immediately after the `initialize` handshake.\n   - Previously, [`server.handle()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/server.py#L104-L188) treated this as an unknown method and returned error `-32601 Method not found: notifications/initialized`.\n   - Per JSON-RPC 2.0 and MCP specifications, notifications (requests without an `id` member) must not receive an error or response.\n   - **Fix**: Handled `notifications/initialized` and generic notifications without returning response bodies (`\"\"`), while returning an empty object result if a client non-standardly supplied an `id`.\n\n3. **`ping` Keep-Alive Support**:\n   - MCP clients often send `ping` requests to check connection liveness. Previously, the server rejected `ping` with `-32601`.\n   - **Fix**: Added handling for [`ping`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/server.py#L170-L171) returning `{}` with the request `id`.\n\n4. **JSON-RPC 2.0 Error Handling \u0026 Robustness**:\n   - Malformed JSON input previously caused uncaught `json.JSONDecodeError` exceptions instead of JSON-RPC `-32700 Parse error`.\n   - Non-object payloads (e.g. primitives, lists) caused uncaught `AttributeError` instead of `-32600 Invalid Request`.\n   - Missing or non-string `method`, invalid `jsonrpc` versions, and non-object `params` now return appropriate standard JSON-RPC error codes (`-32600`, `-32602`).\n   - Null or missing `arguments` in `tools/call` are now handled cleanly rather than throwing `AttributeError`.\n   - Missing `note_id` in `get_note` tool calls now returns an informative error message.\n\n5. **Store Switching in Tests**:\n   - [`server._get_store()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/server.py#L76-L81) now responds dynamically when `PRODUCTION_DB` changes between tests.\n\n---\n\n### Tests Added\n\n- [**`tests/test_server.py`**](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_server.py):\n  - **`TestInitialize`**: Handshake verification, capability advertisement, and protocol version negotiation.\n  - **`TestNotifications`**: Silent handling of `notifications/initialized`, `notifications/cancelled`, and other notifications.\n  - **`TestPing`**: Connection health checks.\n  - **`TestToolsList`**: Tool discovery and schema structure verification.\n  - **`TestToolsCallGetNote`**: Fetching notes, verifying `structuredContent` and `content` match [`NOTE_SCHEMA`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/server.py#L12-L30), missing IDs, and non-existent IDs.\n  - **`TestToolsCallListNotes`**: Listing all notes, filtering by tag, non-existent tag, and verifying [`LIST_SCHEMA`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/server.py#L32-L50).\n  - **`TestToolsCallErrors`**: Unknown tools, malformed arguments, and invalid parameter structures.\n  - **`TestProductionDatabase`**: Live execution with `PRODUCTION_DB=1` verifying serialization and schema compliance with `DynamoStore`.\n  - **`TestJsonRpcProtocolErrors`**: Verification of error codes `-32700`, `-32600`, `-32601`, and `-32602`.\n  - **`TestIdHandling`**: Preservation of string, numeric, and null IDs.\n- [**`tests/test_tools.py`**](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_tools.py):\n  - Added [`GetNoteDynamoStoreTest`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_tools.py#L25-L60) and [`ListNotesDynamoStoreTest`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_tools.py#L76-L88) to verify Decimal coercion and JSON serialization directly against [`DynamoStore`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/db.py#L42-L55).\n  - Added tag edge cases (notes with missing or `None` tags) and [`GetStoreTest`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_tools.py#L90-L108).\n\n### Verification\n\nRun the test suite:\n```bash\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\nOutput:\n```\nRan 49 tests in 0.002s\n\nOK\n```\n","duration_seconds":433.324796,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":358958,"output_tokens":75490,"thinking_tokens":53969,"cache_read_tokens":4705064,"total_tokens":434448}}}
